**Business Development and Publishing Strategy Document**

**Date:** October 5, 2023  
**Prepared by:** Emily Chen, Chief Strategy Officer  
**Company:** Digital Innovations Inc.  

**Overview:**  
Digital Innovations Inc. is positioned to launch its new mobile game, "Adventure Quest," developed by our in-house team led by Game Director James Thompson. The game is set to be released on November 15, 2023, across iOS and Android platforms. Our primary partners for this process include Unity Technologies for development tools, App Store and Google Play for distribution, and AdMob for monetization through ads.

**Development Timeline:**

| Phase               | Start Date   | End Date     | Responsible Entity             |
|---------------------|--------------|--------------|---------------------------------|
| Concept Development  | July 1, 2023 | July 31, 2023 | Game Design Team (Led by Sarah Lee) |
| Alpha Testing        | August 1, 2023 | August 31, 2023 | QA Team (Managed by Mark Johnson) |
| Beta Release        | September 1, 2023 | September 15, 2023 | Marketing Team (Led by Rachel Kim) |
| Final Launch        | November 1, 2023 | November 15, 2023 | All Teams                       |

**Monetization Strategy:**  
Our monetization strategy leverages in-app purchases (IAP) and ad revenues. We anticipate generating $250,000 in the first month post-launch based on historical data from similar titles, such as "Fantasy Realms," which earned $200,000 in its first month. 

**Expected Revenue Breakdown:**

| Revenue Source       | Projected Earnings (First Month) |
|----------------------|-----------------------------------|
| In-App Purchases     | $150,000                          |
| Ad Revenue           | $100,000                          |
| Total Revenue        | $250,000                          |

**Partnerships:**  
- **Unity Technologies:** Provides the game engine and ongoing technical support.
- **AdMob:** Facilitates the integration of advertisements, sharing 70% of the revenue with Digital Innovations.
- **App Store & Google Play:** They will handle distribution, with a 30% commission on all earnings.

